From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 22:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] xinput: Identify the Sony fallback as an Xbox controller

The opt-in Sony hidraw-to-XInput bridge keeps the physical controller's Sony
VID/PID in its hidden WINEXINPUT device. This is needed internally to select
the Sony report translator, but it also leaks through XInputGetCapabilitiesEx.
Games which only accept PlayStation controllers through Steam Input can then
reject the otherwise functional XInput bridge after classifying it as a native
Sony device.

For Sony devices already mapped through the explicit XInput fallback, expose
the capabilities identity of a wired Xbox 360 controller. Keep the underlying
device path unchanged so Wine continues to parse the physical Sony reports
correctly. Native Sony HID devices are unaffected.
---
 dlls/xinput1_3/main.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/xinput1_3/main.c b/dlls/xinput1_3/main.c
--- a/dlls/xinput1_3/main.c
+++ b/dlls/xinput1_3/main.c
@@ -1255,9 +1255,19 @@ DWORD WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH XInputGetCapabilitiesEx(DWORD unk, DWORD index,
         caps->Capabilities.Vibration.wLeftMotorSpeed = 0xff;
         caps->Capabilities.Vibration.wRightMotorSpeed = 0xff;
 
-        caps->VendorId = attr.VendorID;
-        caps->ProductId = attr.ProductID;
         caps->VersionNumber = attr.VersionNumber;
+        if (controllers[index].hid.is_sony_gamepad)
+        {
+            caps->Capabilities.Type = XINPUT_DEVTYPE_GAMEPAD;
+            caps->VendorId = 0x045e;
+            caps->ProductId = 0x028e;
+            TRACE("reporting Sony XInput fallback as Xbox 360 controller.\n");
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            caps->VendorId = attr.VendorID;
+            caps->ProductId = attr.ProductID;
+        }
 
         /* CW-Bug-Id: #23185 Emulate Steam Input native hooks for native SDL */
         if (attr.VendorID == 0x28de && attr.ProductID == 0x11ff)
